<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06565v1/1006ACL1001.png" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/128;" width="476" height="128" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>The overall framework of Auto-Stega.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Web Searcher</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from a library <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> of text steganography strategies, the web searcher uses extensible literature retrieval and information extraction templates to mine recent work and convert candidate methods into executable entries. It evaluates each method with standardized metrics, assigns recommended scenarios, and compares it with existing entries; candidates that exceed the threshold <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are admitted to the lifelong evolving steganographic strategy library.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Steganographic Generator and Evaluator</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a request <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, the system first filters candidate strategies using the “Applicable Scenarios” field recorded in each library entry. It then performs multi-objective ranking of candidates based on evaluation metrics, selects the top-<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> strategies, and uses steganography LLM to generate stego text. The resulting outputs are assessed by the evaluation module; if the predefined acceptance criteria are not met, generation is re-initiated with the next strategy in the ranked set, and the process iterates until the stopping condition is satisfied.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The evaluation module, comprising the detection LLM, which estimates the probability that a given text is steganographic and provides explanatory rationales, and other components, applies predefined criteria, including embedding rate, perplexity (PPL) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mikolov et al. (2010)</a></cite>, and semantic similarity (SS). The embedding rate (ER) can be computed as:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ER=\frac{N_{b}}{W}\," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mi>W</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ER=\frac{N_{b}}{W}\,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of bits in the embedded secret information, and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of words in the stego text. PPL is a common quantitative measure in text generation, defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{PPL}=\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{N_{w}}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{w}}\log p\!\left(w_{i}\mid w_{1},\ldots,w_{i-1}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PPL</mi><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></munderover><mi>log</mi><mpadded style="width:0.333em;" width="0.333em"><mi>p</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PPL}=\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{N_{w}}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{w}}\log p\!\left(w_{i}\mid w_{1},\ldots,w_{i-1}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is the length of the text, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token in text, and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(w_{i}\!\mid\!w_{1},\ldots,w_{i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.052em;" width="0.052em"><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∣</mo></mpadded><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(w_{i}\!\mid\!w_{1},\ldots,w_{i-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability assigned by the language
model to the <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th word given the preceding words. The scorer LLM then compares the response <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and the score <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> produced by the evaluation module against predefined criteria to determine whether the steganographic requirements are satisfied.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06565v1/1002ACL_strategy.png" id="S3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/140;" width="429" height="140" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Steganographic strategy library construction: from warm-up to lifelong learning.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Strategy Library Construction</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The steganographic strategy library <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is organized into two stages: warm-up and lifelong learning. In the warm-up stage, we execute a generate–evaluate loop and log <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T_{s},R,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T_{s},R,S)</annotation></semantics></math> for each request. A summarizer LLM abstracts improvements between nearby or sampled records into structured strategy entries and writes them back to the library <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> after deduplication. Each entry stores motivation, implementation notes, and evaluation summaries. The library <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is maintained as a key–value store whose keys <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> are response embeddings for efficient retrieval. Admission is gated by thresholded scores <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and operational details are given in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.2 Steganographic Generator and Evaluator ‣ 3 Method ‣ Auto-Stega: An Agent-Driven System for Lifelong Strategy Evolution in LLM-Based Text Steganography" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. In the lifelong learning stage, given a request <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and current <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, the system retrieves and ranks candidate strategies, regenerates by evolving new strategies from existing entries in <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> when acceptance criteria are not met, admits improved entries under the same threshold rule, and terminates when scores exceed preset thresholds or the iteration budget is reached. Under the same thresholding rule, the system applies the single-best strategy when it clearly dominates the candidates. When several near-matching strategies jointly satisfy the acceptance criteria, the system assembles them to drive further evolution. When no candidate reaches <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, the system discards the shortlist and initiates alternative discovery. The outputs are the ranked shortlist <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> that is the candidate list constructed during strategy retrieval, and the selected set <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">EFFECTIVE</span>. The procedure is illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.2 Steganographic Generator and Evaluator ‣ 3 Method ‣ Auto-Stega: An Agent-Driven System for Lifelong Strategy Evolution in LLM-Based Text Steganography" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. This compact process turns observed gains into reusable fragments and sustains continual evolution.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Strategy Retrieval and Shortlisting</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            Request <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>; library <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (entry <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> with key <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>); shortlist size <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            Shortlist <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GE</span>: generate and evaluate (outputs <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>); <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">EMB</span>: embed <math id="alg1.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">STS</span>: stable similarity top-<math id="alg1.l3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg1.l3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MD</span>: metric discrepancy vs. current metrics; <span id="alg1.l3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOPK</span>: pick <math id="alg1.l3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> by criterion

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T_{S},R,S)\leftarrow\textsc{GE}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T_{S},R,S)\leftarrow\textsc{GE}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// gen/eval</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{R}\leftarrow\textsc{EMB}(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">EMB</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{R}\leftarrow\textsc{EMB}(R)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// embed</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\leftarrow\textsc{STS}(L,E_{R},2k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">STS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\leftarrow\textsc{STS}(L,E_{R},2k)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// retrieve</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for all</span> <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}\leftarrow\textsc{MD}(j,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">MD</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}\leftarrow\textsc{MD}(j,S)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// score gap</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\leftarrow\textsc{TOPK}(\mathcal{C},\{d_{j}\},k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">TOPK</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\leftarrow\textsc{TOPK}(\mathcal{C},\{d_{j}\},k)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// shortlist</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Strategy Retrieval</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a request <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, the steganographic LLM and the evaluator module produce a stego text, a response, and an overall score <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. We embed the response <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and retrieve the top-<math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k</annotation></semantics></math> entries from <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> by similarity to their keys <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, with stable deterministic tie resolution. The candidates are reranked by metric discrepancy with the current metrics; the best <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> form the shortlist <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that in the first iteration, no response is available for retrieval reference. Thus the steganography LLM is prompted without employing a steganographic strategy in the first iteration. Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.3 Strategy Library Construction ‣ 3 Method ‣ Auto-Stega: An Agent-Driven System for Lifelong Strategy Evolution in LLM-Based Text Steganography" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> formalizes the retrieval and selection procedure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Plug-and-Play High Embedding Rates Mapping</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prior heuristics such as top-<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (nucleus) and locally typical sampling shape the candidate set near the model conditional distribution, improving fluency. However, they lack control over token selection that is calibrated for capacity and aware of the underlying distribution: per-step capacity remains uncalibrated, probability mass is unstructured, and the mapping from bits to tokens is unstable as candidate diversity varies. Accordingly, we propose PC-DNTE (Parity-Constrained Dynamic Nucleus-Typical Encoder).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PC-DNTE</span> is a training free encoder. At each step, it adapts <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[p_{\min},p_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[p_{\min},p_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> to form a nucleus candidate set under <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathrm{ctx}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>ctx</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathrm{ctx}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and applies a local typicality filter; the filtered set is then partitioned into <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=32</annotation></semantics></math> equal mass bins <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{G_{m}\}_{m=0}^{31}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>31</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{G_{m}\}_{m=0}^{31}</annotation></semantics></math>. The choice of <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=32</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that each bin represents a manageable fraction of the total probability mass, allowing the use of a 5 bit index for efficient token selection while preserving the base distribution. The encoder reads <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> ciphertext bits to choose the bin index <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and one parity bit <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and selects tokens in <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> whose seed conditioned parity matches <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding deterministic, seed synchronized decoding. If no such token exists, the algorithm expands <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (within <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p_{\min},p_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p_{\min},p_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>) and retries; if still empty, it records a no embed step, defers the bits, and emits <math id="S3.SS5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max_{y\in G_{m}}p_{\theta}(y\mid\mathrm{ctx}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>ctx</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max_{y\in G_{m}}p_{\theta}(y\mid\mathrm{ctx}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The context is updated after emission. Near sentence boundaries, a small log odds boost to the end of sequence token (EOS) and punctuation together with a bounded closure routine encourages well formed breaks. This adjustment is applied after token emission and also during any no embed closure, and it only reweights the next step candidate set; consequently, it does not modify the bits already embedded. Taken together, the procedure preserves the model conditional distribution, provides deterministic synchronization via seed conditioned parity, and sustains high embedding rates through equal mass binning, with step by step operations in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3.6 Secret Information Extraction ‣ 3 Method ‣ Auto-Stega: An Agent-Driven System for Lifelong Strategy Evolution in LLM-Based Text Steganography" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.6 </span>Secret Information Extraction</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the secret extraction module, when configured with the same steganographic strategy as the encoding side, the decoding LLM is able to accurately decode the embedded secret information.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> PC-DNTE</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            conditional <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathrm{ctx})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ctx</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathrm{ctx})</annotation></semantics></math>; ciphertext <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Bits</span>; <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\min},p_{\max}\!\in\!(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\min},p_{\max}\!\in\!(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>; bins <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{=}32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{=}32</annotation></semantics></math>; scorer <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TYP<math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math></span>; seed <span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Seed</span>; closure <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; budget <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>; punctuation set <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            stego text <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{S}=(t_{1},\ldots,t_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{S}=(t_{1},\ldots,t_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaP</span>: adapt <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\!\in\![p_{\min},p_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\!\in\![p_{\min},p_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DynNuc</span>: nucleus under <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="alg2.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LocTyp</span>: local typicality filter; <span id="alg2.l3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">EqM</span>: split to <math id="alg2.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> equal-mass bins; <span id="alg2.l3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ReadBits</span>: pop <math id="alg2.l3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> bits; <span id="alg2.l3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PH</span>: seed-conditioned parity; <span id="alg2.l3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">IncP</span>: enlarge <math id="alg2.l3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> up to <math id="alg2.l3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg2.l3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">NoEmb</span>: record no-embed; <span id="alg2.l3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">QueueBits</span>: enqueue bits; <span id="alg2.l3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">UpdCtx</span>: update context; <span id="alg2.l3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SBLikely</span>: boundary test; <span id="alg2.l3.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BoostEOS</span>: boost <math id="alg2.l3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg2.l3.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CloseSteps</span>: bounded closure

</div>
